WEBVTT

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:03.130
Detection engineering succeeds through collaboration.

00:00:03.130 --> 00:00:06.840
SOC analysts provide insight into alert quality, investigation workflows,

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:11.140
escalation paths, and operational realities that may not be obvious from the logic alone.

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:13.875
Threat hunters can identify gaps, test hypotheses,

00:00:13.875 --> 00:00:16.300
and reveal emerging opportunities for detection.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:19.410
Incident responders contribute lessons learned from investigations,

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:22.330
including which signals helped and which context was missing.

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:25.720
Strong feedback loops improve both detections and defensive outcomes.

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:30.168
When analysts can report noise, ambiguity, missing fields, or useful context,

00:00:30.168 --> 00:00:33.330
detection engineers can make practical improvements that reduce friction.

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:36.450
Collaboration also improves documentation and usability.

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:40.360
A detection should help the person receiving it understand what happened, why it matters,

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:43.920
and what reasonable next steps might be in the organization’s workflow.
